Wires the new CConnectionTransportP2PWebRTC (see
steamnetworkingsockets_p2p_webrtc_datachannel.h/.cpp, injected as new
source by portfile.cmake, not a patch on existing files) into
CSteamNetworkConnectionP2P, gated on a new STEAMNETWORKINGSOCKETS_ENABLE_WEBRTC_DATACHANNEL
define (separate from Valve's own STEAMNETWORKINGSOCKETS_ENABLE_WEBRTC,
which is their ICE-backend-via-Google's-webrtc.org mechanism -- confirmed
by reading steamnetworkingsockets_p2p_webrtc.h before writing any of this;
that's a different thing, not reused or touched here).

Three files:
- steamnetworkingsockets_p2p.h: new member CConnectionTransportP2PWebRTC
  *m_pTransportWebRTCDataChannel and AttachWebRTCDataChannelTransport()
  declaration, mirroring the ICE/SDR transport members' shape.
- steamnetworkingsockets_p2p.cpp: AttachWebRTCDataChannelTransport()
  implementation (mirrors BInitSDRTransport() -- construct, push onto
  m_vecAvailableTransports), a DestroyTransport() cleanup line, and a new
  ConnectP2PWebRTCDataChannel() entry point mirroring
  ConnectP2PCustomSignaling()/InternalConnectP2P()'s shape but with the
  transport attached between construction and BInitConnect() -- required
  because BInitConnect() checks "is m_vecAvailableTransports empty" and
  fails immediately if so, and InternalConnectP2P's construct-then-
  immediately-BInitConnect sequence has no gap to attach into. v1
  simplification: no symmetric-connect duplicate-connection matching
  (unlike InternalConnectP2P) -- add later if this transport needs it.
- csteamnetworkingsockets.h: ConnectP2PWebRTCDataChannel()'s declaration.
  Deliberately a plain member function, not virtual/override on
  ISteamNetworkingSockets -- keeps this addition off the public ABI
  surface for v1; the coffeecutie application code that calls it includes
  GNS's internal headers directly rather than going through the public
  interface, a deliberate scope-bounding simplification for a first
  working version, not a permanent design commitment.

No patch needed for P2PInternalAcceptConnection() (the remote-accept
counterpart to BInitConnect()): AttachWebRTCDataChannelTransport() just
needs to be called before the application calls AcceptConnection() on the
pending incoming connection, which is already entirely under the
application's control -- P2PInternalAcceptConnection()'s own "any
transports available" check passes for free once that's done, no GNS-side
change required.

